# Security policy — {{ display_name }}

## Reporting
Report suspected vulnerabilities privately to the project owner. Do not open a
public issue for security-sensitive reports.

## Data policy
- Public, non-proprietary inputs only.
- No credentials are required by default; CI runs with no secrets.
- The following must never be committed: API keys, tokens, passwords,
  certificates, employer/customer/partner names, proprietary RTL/logs/waveforms,
  internal hostnames, usernames, or filesystem paths.

## Release
Run the factory's `audit-public-release` (or `scripts` equivalent) before every
public push. See `RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md`.
